            <ArticleTitle>Hindgut Duplication: A Unique Case of Six Perineal Openings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1433</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7759/cureus.1433</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complete hindgut duplication is a rare and intriguing entity, often coupled with genitourinary abnormalities and neural tube defects. The diagnosis demands a thorough clinical exam and radiological workup. Timely recognition and expeditious treatment of these patients can lead to a better quality of life. We present a case of a 10-month-old female with complete hindgut duplication and associated genitourinary duplication treated with surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
